<rml>
<head>
	<title>Generic Confirm Dialog Background</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="generic_confirm_dialog_bg.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
	<!-- Background-context document (see npc_shop_bg.rml for the mechanism) -- paints
	     CCommonMessageBox's own native sprite composite BEFORE the legacy 3D pass draws item3D
	     each frame (RenderBackgroundLayer(), called from CManager::Render() before any
	     window/camera in its z-sorted loop), so the item shows through the gap in
	     generic_confirm_dialog.rml's own now-paint-less #panel instead of being painted over by it
	     (RmlUi's main context, rendered last in the frame, would otherwise always win). No
	     data-model -- #panel centers via plain CSS
	     (left:50%;top:50%;transform:translate(-50%,-50%)); this dialog's position is never
	     C++-computed the way an inventory-family window's is, so there's nothing to sync per
	     frame. -->
	<div id="panel">
		<div class="gcd-bg-sprite-back"></div>
		<div class="gcd-bg-sprite-top"></div>
		<div class="gcd-bg-sprite-middle"></div>
		<div class="gcd-bg-sprite-bottom"></div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
